 The Tile and Slide Framework (Snake-NeRF) is an out-of-core method that scales Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) to massive 3D scenes (e.g., 10km x 10km) by partitioning the volume into non-overlapping 3D tiles, each trained with its own independent NeRF. Unlike sibling methods that dispatch multiple NeRFs across multiple GPUs or require pre-training a global model, this framework operates on a single GPU device, eliminating the need to load all images or network weights simultaneously. It solves the problem of catastrophic forgetting and memory overflow in large-scale training by using a 2x2 sliding window progression and a segmented ray sampler to ensure seamless rendering across tile boundaries.
 
